{"name":"Garden of Earthly Delights","hex":"#a09f5b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"},{"term":"earthly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to the earth or this world, as opposed to heaven or the heavens.","Made of earth; earthy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is of the earth or earthly; a terrestrial being.","A slightest chance (of success etc.) or idea (about something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earthly"},{"term":"delights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of delight"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of delight"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delights"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden of Earthly Delights","blocks":[{"text":"\"Garden of Earthly Delights\" is a song written by Andy Partridge of the English rock band XTC, released as the opening track on their 1989 album Oranges & Lemons. Partridge wrote the song as a children's guide to the world dedicated to his son Harry Partridge. He intended it to sound \"like this crazy tapestry of camels and elephants and belly dancers and all the Arabian Nights, interwoven -- a big ornate Eastern rug come to life.\" It features Arabic modalities and a guitar solo played through two harmonizers set to different intervals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_of_Earthly_Delights","wikidata":"Q60549164"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a 